# Rust Language Support

`Lux.Rust` provides deterministic Rust component definitions for Lux Prisms, Beams, and Lenses.

The support layer focuses on definition, lifecycle, async runtime metadata, Cargo dependency planning, and trait templates. It does not compile or load NIFs by itself; a runtime adapter can execute the generated definitions.

## Inline Rust Component

```elixir
require Lux.Rust

code =
  ~RS'''
  pub fn handle(input: serde_json::Value) -> serde_json::Value {
      input
  }
  '''

Lux.Rust.component_from_code(code,
  name: "ValidationPrism",
  module: "validation_prism",
  kind: :prism
)
```

## Component Definition

```elixir
Lux.Rust.prism_definition(%{
  name: "ValidationPrism",
  module: "validation_prism",
  handler: "handle",
  async: true,
  input_schema: %{type: :object},
  output_schema: %{type: :object}
})
```

## Cargo Manifest

```elixir
Lux.Rust.cargo_manifest(%{
  package: "lux-example",
  dependencies: %{
    "serde" => %{version: "1", features: ["derive"]},
    "serde_json" => "1",
    "tokio" => %{version: "1", features: ["rt", "macros"]}
  }
})
```

## Runtime Plan

```elixir
Lux.Rust.runtime_plan(%{
  async: true,
  max_concurrency: 8,
  queue_limit: 32,
  zero_copy_candidates: [:binary]
})
```

The generated plan includes Tokio runtime metadata, cooperative cancellation, backpressure policy, lifecycle callbacks, JSON input/output encoding, and telemetry hooks.
